    "narrative": "Our primary offensive focus today is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (66.89) and **Jose Caballero** (65.57), both of whom capitalize on high-upside environments. **Corbin Carroll** remains a top-tier start despite the dynamic platoon disadvantage against Connor Prielipp, as his projected volume in the #3 hole and overall elite toolset keep his floor elevated. Meanwhile, **Jose Caballero** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Rhett Lowder (xERA 5.10); the combination of favorable wind conditions and the high-skill-gap matchup outweighs his platoon penalty, making him a critical engine for stolen bases today. **Tyler Soderstrom** (65.47) also earns a strong recommendation, as his projection is bolstered by a 10% park factor bump and a favorable dynamic platoon split against the right-handed Jos\u00e9 Soriano.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros**, who posted a respectable 48.97 but ultimately fell short due to his anticipated #9 spot in the order and the lack of a confirmed lineup. While **Kyle Karros** offers a massive 14% park-factor surge, the optimizer favored the higher daily efficiency scores of **Dalton Rushing** (60.79) and **Alex Freeland** (54.80), despite their lower spots in the order, because their SP matchups against Trey Gibson provide higher probability for counting stats. **Austin Riley** (45.88) was also considered, but his match against the high-velocity Jacob Misiorowski (xERA 2.70) suppresses his ceiling, keeping him on the bench to preserve our game cap limit. \n\nA final word of caution: while we are high on the volume for **Travis Bazzana** (61.45) at the top of the lineup against Tatsuya Imai, our overall roster efficiency is heavily dependent on these \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. Should **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, or **Josh Naylor** slide down their respective orders once confirmed, their efficiency scores will regress. Monitor the wind reports closely, particularly for **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Jose Caballero**, as the current \"Wind Out\" projection is the primary catalyst keeping those scores in the strong category.",
